    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Client types and functions for the 014 contract (list fields, `creatableEventTypes`, get event, patch event, assignable people).</step>
    <step order="2">Add event dialog: type dropdown, required-by-type due date, priority, assignee, description; remove the radio.</step>
    <step order="3">`sprk_event` record template; open from an Events row via ChildRecordModal; deep link.</step>
    <step order="4">Edit and Change status child dialogs; refresh the record and the parent Events list after save.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: type required; due date by type; options only from the BFF; View Only sees no Edit/Change status; Collaborate sees both; focus returns to the row; one-level rule; deep link reader vs not-found.</step>
    <step order="6">typecheck, lint, vitest, build; TASK-INDEX, POML status, drift check, notes.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>EventsCalendar create dialog; record template + ChildRecordModal; FormModal child-dialog hosts in `record/actions/`.</existing>
    <extension>Yes: a seventh template config entry and two action hosts following the existing pattern; no new shared component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Events cannot be typed, opened, linked, edited or completed by external users (owner Q-1–Q-7).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Add event cannot be submitted without a type; the type options are exactly `creatableEventTypes`; a type that requires a due date blocks submit without one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A created event shows its type, priority, assignee and description in the list and on its record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Clicking an Events row opens the event over the record (the record stays mounted); Close returns focus to the row; `?record=event:{id}` opens it top-level, and a non-readable id shows the not-found state.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A View Only caller sees no Edit or Change status; a Collaborate caller sees both; Edit shows the type read-only; Change status offers `allowedStatuses`; after a save the record and the Events list show the new values.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">typecheck, lint, vitest and build pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

